<title>THAILAND: Thai Banpu invests in Indonesian coal.</title>
<headline>Thai Banpu invests in Indonesian coal.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banpu Plc, a major Thai coal miner and importer, will invest nearly US$1 million in an Indonesian coal company, the company said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>Banpu's board of directors had agreed to buy 285 shares of PT Jorong Baruntama Greston of Indonesia at a price of around $3,333.33 per share, it said in a filing to the Thai stock exchange. -- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
